    "name": "6 Hours Welcome to Brisbane Private Tours - Our Top Picks",
    "shortDescription": "Your price starts from A$118 per person! You'll explore Brisbane's popular sights and hidden gems! For early arrival, Brisbane airport or cruise port pick-up and drop-off available.",
    "description": "<p><b><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-large\">Overview</span></b><br></p><p><b>Best of Queensland Experiences Award</b></p><p><b>Google Review ★★★★★ 5.0 (78) Tripadvisor ★★★★★ 5.0 (32)</b></p><p>With flexibility on pickup times, premium vehicles, and additional stops according to your interests, we head straight up to Mt.Coot-tha to enjoy the stunning views of Brisbane. Take a break at the cafe while enjoying the view. Next, we’ll stop at South Bank, where you can visit the famous BRISBANE sign or ride the ferris wheel then check out&nbsp; the man-made lagoon while looking across the city. At Kangaroo Point Cliffs, capture the scenic views of the river and city. Followed by Captain Burke Park located under the Story Bridge, for a unique view of this iconic structure. Finally, Wilson’s Lookout offers a quiet place to see the city’s best skyline views. It’s a great spot for wrapping up your best day tour! If we have time we can show you more!&nbsp;</p><p><b>Price</b> |&nbsp;&nbsp;From A$118 per person to A$1195 per person, depending on your group size.</p><p><b>Vehicle</b>&nbsp;|&nbsp; 1-3 guests: Luxurious Car, (4-6 guests Vito*), 7-11 guests, Mini-bus *subject to availability<br></p><p><b>Time</b> |&nbsp; Morning, Afternoon, or Twilight</p><p><b>Duration</b> |&nbsp; approx. 6 hrs</p><p><br></p><p class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-left\"><b><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-large\">Destinations</span></b></p><p><b>⚲ Pick-up at your preferred location&nbsp;</b><b>within Brisbane&nbsp; (airport or cruise terminal pick- up extra charge )</b></p><p>⁞<br></p><p><b>⚲ 1.&nbsp;&nbsp;Mt. Coot-Tha&nbsp;</b></p><p>Experience 360-degree panoramic views of Brisbane City from one of its most iconic lookouts, Mt. Coot-tha. Bring your camera and capture stunning photos as you gaze out over the skyline towards Moreton Bay in the distance. You can enjoy a refreshing stop with ice cream or coffee, perfect for taking in the natural beauty and tranquillity of the area.</p><p>⁞<br></p><p><b>⚲ 2.&nbsp;&nbsp;Mt. Coot-Tha Botanic Gardens</b></p><p>Our return journey from Mount Coot-tha includes a curated stop at the Brisbane Botanic Gardens. We begin at the climate-controlled Tropical Display Dome and the lush Fern House before moving to the tranquil Japanese Gardens and the Bonsai House. The experience concludes with a short walk through a miniature tropical rainforest.&nbsp;</p><p>⁞</p><p><b>⚲ 3.&nbsp; South Bank Parklands and Lagoon Beach</b></p><p>You'll see some of Brisbane's cultural landmarks, including the Ferris Wheel and the iconic beach-style lagoon. Take a selfie by the famous BRISBANE sign and take a dip at the man-made lagoon while taking in the stunning views of the city and Brisbane's latest landmark, the Queens Wharf Development. There's a shopping area where you can grab a bite or snag some souvenirs.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>⁞</p><p><b>⚲ 4.&nbsp; Kangaroo Point Cliffs</b></p><p>At Kangaroo Point Cliffs, you will see the stunning views of the Brisbane River and skyline. These ancient cliffs formed from volcanic rock provide the perfect spot for photos and refreshment. Let yourself enjoy a moment to soak in the beauty of the city from the cliffs! Twilight time is highly recommended to capture when the city lights begin to sparkle!</p><p>⁞<br></p><p><b>⚲ 5.&nbsp; Captain Burke Park under the Story Bridge</b></p><p>Located beneath the iconic Story Bridge, Captain Burke Park offers a unique perspective of one of Brisbane’s popular landmarks. Feel the breeze as you take in the impressive architecture of the bridge while enjoying the serene riverside location. It’s a fantastic stop for those who appreciate history and scenic views!</p><p>⁞<br></p><p>Drive by Story Bridge</p><p>⁞</p><p><b>⚲ 6.&nbsp; Wilson's Lookout</b></p><p>For a more intimate vantage point, Wilson’s Lookout offers sweeping views of the Brisbane River and Story Bridge. Tucked away in a quiet residential area, this lookout offers a peaceful stop, ideal for photography enthusiasts looking to capture the city from a different angle. Best spot for taking light-up city view!</p><p>⁞</p><p>Drive by Fellons Brewery</p><p>Drive through Brisbane City and historical buildings</p><p>⁞</p><p><b>⚲&nbsp;Drop-off at your preferred location within Brisbane City</b></p><p><b><br></b></p><p><b>* From/To Airport / Cruise Terminal: $120 per way</b></p><p><b>* Gold Coast Hotel Transfers: $390</b></p><p><br></p><p><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-large\"><b>What’s Included</b></span></p><p>✔︎&nbsp; Live Commentary On-board&nbsp; ✔︎&nbsp; Gift Pack (bottled water, snacks and more!)&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>✔︎&nbsp; Flexible Itineraries&nbsp; ✔︎&nbsp; Combination Pick-up/Drop-off</p><p><br></p><p><b><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-large\">What's&nbsp;</span><u><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-large\">Not</span></u><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-large\">&nbsp;Included</span></b></p><p>✖︎&nbsp; Personal Expenses (e.g. meal, extra activities)&nbsp;<br></p><p></p><p><br></p><p><b><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-large\">Please Note</span></b></p><p>•&nbsp; It is your tour, we are flexible on pick-up/drop-off locations, start time, and itineraries! Please let us know what you like!</p><p>•&nbsp; Brisbane Airport / Cruise Terminal pick-up and drop-off is available for additional cost. Please select an extra in the next page.</p><p>•&nbsp; Use this as a base tour, and you can make changes to the itinerary.<br></p><p>•&nbsp; Please enquire about the price for larger groups.</p><p>•&nbsp; Free cancellation policy applies&nbsp;outside of 24 hours of the scheduled tour departure.</p><p><br></p><p><b><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-large\">Find Us</span></b></p><p>☏ |&nbsp; (+61) 400 055 199</p><p>✉︎ |&nbsp; info@adventuredaytrips.com.au</p><p>Website |&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"http://www.adventuredaytrips.com.au/\">adventuredaytrips.com.au</a></p><p>Reviews |&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"http://www.google.com/search?q=adventuredaytrips+google+review&amp;rlz=1C1VDKB_en-GBAU972AU972&amp;oq=adventuredaytrips+&amp;gs_lcrp=EgZjaHJvbWUqCAgAEEUYJxg7MggIABBFGCcYOzIGCAEQRRg7MgYIAhBFGDkyBggDEEUYQTIGCAQQRRg8MgYIBRBFGEEyBggGEEUYPDIGCAcQRRg8qAIAsAIB&amp;sourceid=chrome&amp;ie=UTF-8#lrd=0x6b9157412d20e55f:0x183b6186c3517619,1\">Google Review</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"http://www.tripadvisor.com.au/Attraction_Review-g255068-d19793376-Reviews-Adventure_Day_Trips_Brisbane-Brisbane_Brisbane_Region_Queensland.html\">Tripadvisor</a></p><p>Instagram |&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"http://www.instagram.com/adventuredaytripsbrisbane/\">@adventuredaytripsbrisbane</a></p><p>Facebook |&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/adventuredaytripsQueensland\">Adventure Day Trips Brisbane</a></p>",
